hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1520","I am Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, we are Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi, Aban bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Badil al-Uqaili, Abu Attiya is a man from among us, and Salam bin Junada told us, Waki` told us, on the authority of Aban bin Yazid Al-Attar, on the authority of Budil bin Maysarah Al-Uqaili, On the authority of a man among them who was nicknamed Abu Atiyya, and this is the hadith of Al-Dawrqi. He said: Malik bin Al-Huwayrith came to us, and the time for prayer came, and he was told: Come forward. He said: Let a man from among you lead you. When they prayed, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If a man visits the people, he should not lead them in prayer. And let a man from among them lead them.” In a hadith by Waki`, he said: “Let some of you come forward, so I can tell you why I don’t come forward.”"
